Phase 3.7 — M3.4 headless LSP bridge + Phase 3 exit
========================================================================
Node: M3.4 (headless LSP diagnostics/symbol bridge)
Plan authority: docs/18 § Concrete local indexing stack ("Semantic
language services: headless LSP processes normalized into Modbit
diagnostics/symbol records") + the fallback invariant ("If semantic
embedding is unavailable, exact/BM25/AST/LSP remain fully functional";
here: LSP itself is the optional input and the deterministic
tree-sitter surface is the always-on backbone)
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 3 — final milestone card before the
exit record
Revisions: the M3.4 commit (lsp.rs + lsp-fixture + TaskIndexWriter
enrichment + E2E) and the closure commit on main
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: modbit-diagnostics was logic-only
pull-diagnostics with zero LSP code and zero product callers)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- crates/diagnostics/src/lsp.rs (new): minimal headless LSP client —
  Content-Length-framed JSON-RPC over stdio, initialize handshake +
  initialized notification, didOpen (once per file per session),
  textDocument/definition and textDocument/references, answers
  normalized to worktree-relative 1-based locations, typed errors
  (spawn/io/timeout/server/closed), bounded requests (10 s in
  production), kill-on-drop. FAIL-SOFT by design: every failure is
  typed and every caller degrades to the deterministic tree-sitter
  surface (docs/18 fallback invariant).
- lsp-fixture bin (new): a REAL wire-protocol peer — a framed JSON-RPC
  server with canned semantic answers resolved against didOpen'd
  document text (word-at-position lookup, null answers for non-symbol
  positions, includeDeclaration honored). The bridge is tested against
  an actual protocol peer on every CI runner with NO language-server
  installation.
- crates/core-runtime: modbit-diagnostics enters the product closure
  (17 → 18 of 26). TaskIndexWriter gains a lazy per-language LSP
  session pool (MODBIT_LSP_RUST/_TYPESCRIPT/_JAVASCRIPT/_PYTHON env
  commands; spawn failures cached so a missing binary is not retried
  per query); search.symbol enriches the tree-sitter answer with the
  LSP definition/references section — ANY LSP failure degrades to an
  explicit {"unavailable": reason} note and the tool never fails
  because LSP did. The planner's L2 structural route serves through
  the same surface (search.symbol IS the L2 answer path).
- E2E (daemon_context_query_e2e): the daemon runs with the fixture as
  a REAL wire peer (MODBIT_LSP_RUST=target/debug/lsp-fixture); turn 2's
  durable conversation carries the lsp section — server provenance,
  the null-definition path (the fixture only knows its own symbol),
  and a normalized cross-document reference.
- Bridge integration (crates/diagnostics/tests/lsp_bridge.rs):
  handshake + didOpen + definition (call site → defining line) +
  references (same-document and cross-document, includeDeclaration
  honored) + idempotent didOpen against the fixture; a real
  rust-analyzer smoke runs ONLY when the binary is installed and is
  bounded to the handshake claim (semantic queries need full indexing —
  not gated).

